    "notes": "Ringve Music Museum’s main manor house, Hovedbygningen, as seen in September 2009 before the 2015 fire. Includes the long wooden range, projecting garden room, two unequal towers, and attached entrances at either end. The separate stable, Wessel building, arboretum and exhibition interiors are outside this model. The ground plan is from the current mapping of the restored building. Preserved external footprints are interpreted alongside the pre-fire photographs."
